00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.075
JONATHAN LIEBERMAN: For us it
came down to three choices.

00:12:06.075 --> 00:12:09.340
First of all, we looked at
everything in the market.

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.980
And at the end of
the day, Google

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.890
stood tallest when it came
to performance, price,

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:17.290
and your technology.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.570
From a performance
standpoint, we

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:24.970
recognize and understand
that your Google Cloud

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.490
is the same thing that
runs G Suite, that

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:31.330
runs your search, that runs your
maps, everything, the lowest

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.130
latency in the market.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:36.640
And for our service,
you need a low latency.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.370
And so having data centers
throughout the world

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:42.617
is a very key differentiator
that we looked at.

00:12:42.617 --> 00:12:44.950
From a price point of view,
you bill down to the minute,

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.280
compared with the others
that bill on an hourly basis.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.240
And then from a
technology point of view,

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.510
everything that you're
doing, from machine learning

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:57.120
to AI to everything else, was
also very important to us,

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.500
as we want to deliver the
most innovative services

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.324
to our customers.

00:13:00.324 --> 00:13:01.240
